// error
// #6026: the bare `{}` map literal has the identical shape as the empty
// slice literal `[]` (check_empty_slicelit_noncollection.bit) — its own
// inferred type is invalid (`checkMapLit`, checkbindexpr.bit, answers `0`
// for zero entries), so a KNOWN, non-map expected type used to pass `bit
// check` clean and fail only at lowering (E0092, "cannot lower a map
// literal whose target type is not a map"). One E0041 per context
// `vExpectExpr` pushes an expectation into: a function argument, a `let`
// annotation and a struct field initializer — `return {}` is left to the
// slice fixture's identical `vExpectSliceLit`/`vExpectMapLit` shape, since a
// bare `{}` cannot be written as a `return` value at all here: `return`
// parsed with no following expression (`canStartExpression`,
// parserstmt.bit, excludes `Kind.LBrace`, so `return {}` is a bare
// `return` plus a stray block) and `bit fmt` strips the parens that would
// otherwise disambiguate `return ({})`, reintroducing the same parse
// error — a separate fmt defect, filed apart from this ticket.
class Box {
  v: string,
}

fn take(s: string) {}

fn main() {
  take({})
  let x: string = {}
  let b = Box{ v = {} }
  println(x + b.v)
}
